# Machine: what the program runs on. The logical core count the parallel walk sizes its pool by, and the platform and
# architecture names, spelled as node's `os.platform()` and `os.arch()` spell them on every backend (`darwin`, `linux`,
# `win32`; `arm64`, `x64`), so a program branches on one set of names. The implementation is selected at build time per
# platform and hidden behind this API.

mark unstable

load @term/base/native/{platform}/machine
  find host-cores
  find host-platform
  find host-architecture
  find host-runtime

# the logical processors, at least 1
task count-cores
  like number
  send back
    call host-cores

# `darwin`, `linux`, `win32`, as node's `os.platform()` names them
task read-platform
  like text
  send back
    call host-platform

# `arm64`, `x64`, as node's `os.arch()` names them
task read-architecture
  like text
  send back
    call host-architecture

# the runtime running the program: `node v22.23.4` on node (`node`, a space, its version), `rust` and `swift` for a
# compiled binary, `jvm 21.0.4` on kotlin (`jvm`, a space, the JVM's `java.version`)
task read-runtime
  like text
  send back
    call host-runtime
